    "sha": "35ccd09ff54ebe2ec6dfea06211796abbd4d5426",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOV1WsOtoAKDM1Y2NkMDlmZjU0ZWJlMmVjNmRmZWEwNjIxMTc5NmFiYmQ0ZDU0MjY",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "Quintin Smits",
        "email": "qd.smits@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-25T11:03:49Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "Quintin Smits",
        "email": "qd.smits@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-25T11:03:49Z"
      },
      "message": "feat(multiaxis): start and exit picks for the 5-axis contour\n\nThe 5-Axis Contour takes a start point and an exit point\n(PickCapability::Ring). Each closed waterline ring is re-sequenced to\nbegin at its point nearest the start pick, and after its lap runs on to\nits point nearest the exit pick. The cut order and geometry do not\nchange; the stamp, the shank dodge and the centre-cutting guard judge\nthe seated path. A pick far from every ring, a ladder with no closed\nring, and a blocked plunge or retract column at the pick are refused by\nname. A path without a pick is byte-identical.\n\nRefs #3330\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
